<title>EGYPT: Yield rises on Egyptian 182-day treasury bills.</title>
<headline>Yield rises on Egyptian 182-day treasury bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 182-day treasury bills rose to 9.631 percent on Monday from 9.606 percent at the previous auction on April 7.</p>
<p>The new bills, with a value of 878.375 million pounds, replace bills worth 657.025 million maturing on Tuesday. The treasury had asked for 800 million pounds.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: Oct 21, 1997 (Oct 7, 1997).</p>
<p>Average yield: 9.631 percent (9.606).</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 878.375 million (879.875 million).</p>
<p>Value of bids: 1,045.125 million (1,820.275 million).</p>
<p>Range accepted: 9.000-9.738 percent (9.000-9.641).</p>
<p>Range of bids: 9.000-10.200 percent (9.000-10.050).</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 114 (54).</p>
<p>Number of bids: 133 (197).</p>
<p>$1 = 3.395 pounds.</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1/</p>
